    "title": "pandas.tseries.offsets.HalfYearEnd.name — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.tseries.offsets.HalfYearEnd.name#\n\n- HalfYearEnd.name#\n- Return a string representing the base frequency. Deprecated since version 3.1.0: The `.name` property is deprecated. Use`.rule_code` instead.This is typically a short string alias (e.g., ‘h’ for hourly, ‘D’ for daily) used to identify the offset type, regardless of the n multiplier. See also \n  - `tseries.offsets.Week`\n  - Represents a weekly offset.\n  - `DateOffset`\n  - Base class for all other offset classes.\n  - `tseries.offsets.Day`\n  - Represents a single day offset.\n  - `tseries.offsets.MonthEnd`\n  - Represents a monthly offset that snaps to the end of the month.\n Examples >>> pd.offsets.Hour().name 'h' >>> pd.offsets.Hour(5).name 'h'",
    "markdown_length": 714,
